<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gonzalo Sánchez de Lozada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1930</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gonzalo Sánchez de Lozada was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> from 1993 to 1997 and from 2002 to 2003. As planning minister in 1985 he designed the New Economic Policy that ended hyperinflation. In his first term he partly privatised state companies and decentralised government. In October 2003 the Gas War protests, in which dozens of people were killed by security forces, forced him to resign and flee to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gonzalo-sanchez-de-lozada.jpg" alt="Gonzalo Sánchez de Lozada" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antônio Cruz/ABr · CC BY 3.0 br · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gonz%C3%A1lo_S%C3%A1nchez_de_Lozada-Agencia_BrasilAntonio_Cruz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
